here were six suppressions in the repo that either said nothing (`// biome-ignore lint:`) or still carried biome's `<explanation>` placeholder. A bare `biome-ignore lint:` silences every rule at that line, so the next real violation to appear there goes unreported. Each one now names the rule it suppresses and why.\n\nTwo of them turned out to be unnecessary. `DATA` in `packages/bench/object-setup.ts` is only ever imported, never reassigned, so it's `const` now — and the `noInnerDeclarations` ignore stacked above it never fired at all, since the declaration is top-level. The compile fuzzer also had a `catch (e)` binding it doesn't use, which was tripping `noUnusedVariables` with no suppression at all.\n\nI confirmed each rule name against biome's actual output rather than taking them on faith, and verified the two rationales that make a claim: `errorUtil.toString` has 31 call sites in v3, and dropping `export` from `RecursiveA` makes `tsc` fail with TS6196 under `noUnusedLocals`, which is what that export is there for.\n\nNo behavior changes. The two `core/` files are comment-only, so all three axes are untouched.\n\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/actions/runs/33268327091/job/99142234577) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `Claude Opus` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-29T18:33:34Z","updated_at":"2026-08-29T19:52:49Z","closed_at":"2026-08-29T19:52:47Z","merged_at":"2026-08-29T19:52:46Z","merge_commit_sha":"c46eeff050f2a6a2ba8db1d14c2c8247bd7623f2","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"